  "notes": [
    "Nine native FX/pending-state bodies (1316 bytes) join the previous sixteen (4332 bytes), entirely in private memory. Complete normalized bodies and dependency/global roles verified on both local images; five altered-state controls rejected on each.",
    "Actual native getter/Begin/Pass/Dynamic/End/binder/walker use a live D3DX27 effect. Dirty vertex/index buffer application uses actual native state code and COM calls, with wrong-binding controls and exact masks/counters in both skip modes.",
    "Material/source computation, ready asset, texture-holder-empty list, geometry/state objects and lifetimes remain controlled. Fixed-function material/light/texture/shader paths are not exercised by these GPU cases.",
    "Fault reference draws all 25 native meshes without plugin instancing. The unchanged baseline instancer was observed to leak the null-stream offset, so it cannot be the exact-state recovery reference.",
    "240 rejected batch operations (14 original positions plus null-stream pre-unbind restore) and eight leader capture failures pass output/state/count/ABI/ownership checks. Immediate state includes native render/SAS/method fields and actual effect parameter values including bones.",
    "Sixteen broken controls rejected: corrupt count, omitted replay, duplicate committed replay, missing null-stream offset restore. Ordinary replay remains direct GPU submission and never mutates D3DX source values.",
    "Two serial guarded timing repeats, 21 alternating-order samples after four warmups, each eight fenced regular/extra pairs. Includes native lifecycle/state and final offset restoration. Lit/shadow alternative full workloads, never additive.",
    "Exploratory initial/debug runs stopped before timing due to a history-dependent synthetic early DIP; restored its explicit palette commit. controls-1 exploratory timing precedes the offset fix and is excluded.",
    "recovery-final log is excluded because a fourth negative launcher case was added while the old executable was in use; qualified log reruns all four controls on rebuilt code.",
    "No production source/install/INI/stable branch changes, no game startup or gameplay FPS claim. Persistent/multiple/device-loss, nondeferred/rigid/verification recovery, source computations/lifetimes and native exceptions remain unqualified."
  ]
